<title>USA: U.S. investigators to leave for Guam - Pentagon.</title>
<headline>U.S. investigators to leave for Guam - Pentagon.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Defence Department said on Tuesday it would fly a National Transportation Safety Board team to Guam to investigate the crash of a Korean Air Lines Boeing 747.</p>
<p>The NTSB team was to fly out of Andrews Air Force Base near Washington aboard an Air Force C-141 &quot;Starlifter&quot; heavy transport aircraft, a Pentagon spokesman, Army Col. Dick Bridges, said.</p>
<p>The NTSB, the independent federal agency that investigates transportation accidents, said it was putting together its investigative team.</p>
